data.content:
Here's the output:

```json
{
  "Name": "alice",
  "Age": 30
}
```

The key piece is `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` — added in .NET 9 as a built-in policy. Since C# record positional parameters are lowercased by convention (`name`, `age`), this policy converts them to `Name` and `Age` in the JSON.

Full program (`Program.cs`):

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("alice", 30);

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase,
    WriteIndented = true
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string name, int age);
```
